{"id":"mimid-e13m.18","title":"auth 18: tailnet deny list and the cross-session /msg mimid tailnet listing","description":"Left out of bead mimid-e13m.12, which built the rest of docs/design/frontend-auth.md §4.6. Two pieces, both needing state the front end does not have today:

1. `/msg mimid tailnet deny <node>` and the deny list §4.6 describes: a persisted list in the agent's database, so it survives a restart. That means a new table in mimid-agent-store, which owns the agent's tables, and a hook that closes the denied node's sessions (and, once Matrix exists, deletes its devices). §4.6 itself says the real revocation is removing the node in the tailnet admin console, which bead mimid-e13m.12 already honours within recheck_s.

2. `/msg mimid tailnet` listing EVERY matched node with its open sessions. What shipped answers for the asking connection alone, because mimid-agent-irc keeps no registry of open sessions: connections live in a JoinSet and nothing can enumerate them. A registry is the work here, and it would also serve a `/msg mimid sessions` for credential sessions.","status":"open","priority":3,"issue_type":"task","owner":"mark@reviewcommit.com","created_at":"2026-11-24T17:08:56.352617739Z","created_by":"Mark Atwood","updated_at":"2026-11-24T17:08:56.352617739Z","labels":["auth","agent"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"mimid-e13m.18","depends_on_id":"mimid-e13m","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-11-24T17:08:56.392826741Z","created_by":"Mark Atwood","metadata":"{}"}]}
